data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":804,"output_index":1,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_004211fe2f756aed016aca518849008196a97ca0c611a178ec","call_id":"call_ef959c725eaa4902bf078566b4b5276c","name":"edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"server.js\",\"edits\":[{\"oldText\":\"  created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\\n);\\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tasks\",\"newText\":\"  created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\\n  archived INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0\\n);\\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tasks\"},{\"oldText\":\"`);\\n\\nconst send\",\"newText\":\"`);\\n// Upgrade databases created before project archiving was introduced.\\nconst projectColumns = db.prepare('PRAGMA table_info(projects)').all();\\nif (!projectColumns.some(column => column.name === 'archived')) db.exec('ALTER TABLE projects ADD COLUMN archived INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0');\\n\\nconst send\"},{\"oldText\":\"return send(res, 200, db.prepare('SELECT id, name FROM projects ORDER BY id ASC').all());\",\"newText\":\"return send(res, 200, db.prepare(`SELECT p.id, p.name, p.archived,\\n      COUNT(t.id) AS total_count, COALESCE(SUM(t.completed), 0) AS completed_count\\n      FROM projects p LEFT JOIN tasks t ON t.project_id = p.id\\n      GROUP BY p.id ORDER BY p.id ASC`).all().map(p => ({ ...p, archived: !!p.archived, summary: `${p.completed_count}/${p.total_count} completed` })));\"},{\"oldText\":\"  const taskListMatch = url.pathname.match(/^\\\\/api\\\\/projects\\\\/(\\\\d+)\\\\/tasks$/);\",\"newText\":\"  const archiveMatch = url.pathname.match(/^\\\\/api\\\\/projects\\\\/(\\\\d+)\\\\/(archive|restore)$/);\\n  if (archiveMatch && req.method === 'POST') {\\n    const changed = db.prepare('UPDATE projects SET archived = ? WHERE id = ?').run(archiveMatch[2] === 'archive' ? 1 : 0, Number(archiveMatch[1]));\\n    return changed.changes ? send(res, 200, { ok: true }) : send(res, 404, { error: 'Project not found' });\\n  }\\n  const taskListMatch = url.pathname.match(/^\\\\/api\\\\/projects\\\\/(\\\\d+)\\\\/tasks$/);\"},{\"oldText\":\"if (!db.prepare('SELECT id FROM projects WHERE id = ?').get(projectId)) return send(res, 404, { error: 'Project not found' });\",\"newText\":\"const owner = db.prepare('SELECT id, archived FROM projects WHERE id = ?').get(projectId);\\n      if (!owner) return send(res, 404, { error: 'Project not found' });\\n      if (owner.archived) return send(res, 403, { error: 'Archived projects cannot have tasks' });\"},{\"oldText\":\"const result = db.prepare('UPDATE tasks SET completed = ? WHERE id = ?').run(body.completed ? 1 : 0, Number(taskMatch[1]));\",\"newText\":\"const result = db.prepare(`UPDATE tasks SET completed = ? WHERE id = ? AND project_id IN\\n        (SELECT id FROM projects WHERE archived = 0)`).run(body.completed ? 1 : 0, Number(taskMatch[1]));\"},{\"oldText\":\"const project = db.prepare('SELECT id, name FROM projects WHERE id = ?').get(Number(projectMatch[1]));\\n    return project ? send(res, 200, project) : send(res, 404, { error: 'Project not found' });\",\"newText\":\"const project = db.prepare('SELECT id, name, archived FROM projects WHERE id = ?').get(Number(projectMatch[1]));\\n    return project ? send(res, 200, { ...project, archived: !!project.archived }) : send(res, 404, { error: 'Project not found' });\"}]}","status":"completed"}}

event: response.completed
data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":805,"response":{"id":"resp_004211fe2f756aed016aca5185d1d481969bbf543bd091b87b","object":"response","created_at":1791644037,"completed_at":1791644043,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6-luna","access_programs":null,"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You are an expert coding assistant operating inside pi, a coding agent harness. You help users by reading files, executing commands, editing code, and writing new files.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nIn addition to the tools above, you may have access to other custom tools depending on the project.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for precise changes (edits[].oldText must match exactly)\n- When changing multiple separate locations in one file, use one edit call with multiple entries in edits[] instead of multiple edit calls\n- Each edits[].oldText is matched against the original file, not after earlier edits are applied. Do not emit overlapping or nested edits. Merge nearby changes into one edit.\n- Keep edits[].oldText as small as possible while still being unique in the file. Do not pad with large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about pi itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), pi packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- When working on pi topics, read the docs and examples, and follow .md cross-references before implementing\n- Always read pi .md files completely and follow links to related docs (e.g., tui.md for TUI API details)\n</docs>\n\n<cwd>\n/home/agent/work\n</cwd>","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_004211fe2f756aed016aca518675e48196b7941529d7498799","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Implementing archive migration**"}],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqylGIwxAG0lB2BxPMVAPlCEkfTjRsJce-u4LChM3cJo2YraprUgrvdnE94_5IcIieDcMUkxxD9rIkkf_tPraJYpK_jHMs6NdSKT5vJZp4USFEtDFTQLp62HzkwIAPGxiwADMEl_4JZXmIaXfmsOhygtM3-kC_MeDaWKSKD6Ul10cBtPupWfly_qSUC45znXx6qQVjx4cNVCrqfKnMnbvLMRF_Y4bFlrHp8czSfMIAlFH1twzGC8jyHUWdqfM3WPlI5I0_LOWnzrdORaL71WgnbkWU820VdM5v30cDU2vR1kNSQ4PeD3OgK1aBhA1d5m0GjFM224FN7MDUR3aovOI4EXZv5_l5Vj2UqdrjOE6sP3dWdGrEZ0aX-QsKcRYQrY7CLcRzLGarHAgQjPGjVlPjr592XYpdG7jZnYNo_IPdwxjdp-jFBM8Ibisbt3Wh_NnoyYWndCe-K3Vjn6G-odnVRruq-HhlR1gZmYL1uldE-Tjd-Y7hbq3upH7Az6NjvVrll6j-KfC78vUmrtsncjUMppajZN5iZkf3RjseyL241CNyeSAlie08yEDnNs-Ytgliac6RiGiLdkZ-SM6YzaFG9lf